    "correct_option": "Source gNB-CU-CP sends RRCReconfiguration via the source gNB-DU to the UE; target gNB-DU sends RRCReconfigurationComplete to target gNB-CU-CP",
    "evidence": "TS 38.401 §8.2.1.1/8.9.4: Source gNB-CU-CP sends HANDOVER REQUEST → target gNB-CU-CP responds with HANDOVER REQUEST ACKNOWLEDGE → F1 UE Context Modification carries the RRCReconfiguration to the UE → RACH and RRCReconfigurationComplete to target gNB-DU → target sends UP RRC MESSAGE TRANSFER to gNB-CU.",
    "source": "TS 38.401 8.2.1.1, 8.9.4"
  },
  {
    "id": "q_6057",
    "verdict": "correct",
    "correct_option": "The voice session is moved from PS/access IMS to CS circuit voice with session continuity provided by SCC AS",
    "evidence": "TS 23.216 specifies SRVCC architecture: voice is anchored in IMS (SCC AS), and the voice leg is moved from E-UTRAN IMS/PS to UTRAN/GERAN CS during handover so the call continues. The MSC server initiates the CS call to the STN-SR which routes to SCC AS to perform the session transfer.",
    "source": "TS 23.216 4.1, 4.2"
  },
  {
    "id": "q_6061",
    "verdict": "correct",
    "correct_option": "If sent in response to BlockAckReq, Duration/ID is the value from the immediate BlockAckReq frame minus the time required to transmit the BlockAck and its SIFS interval",
    "evidence": "IEEE 802.11 §7.2.1.8 (BlockAck frame format) states: 'If the BlockAck frame is sent in response to the BlockAckReq frame, the Duration/ID field value is the value obtained from the Duration/ID field of the immediate BlockAckReq frame, minus the time, in microseconds, required to transmit the BlockAck frame and its SIFS interval.'",
    "source": "IEEE 802.11-2007 7.2.1.8"
  },
